⭐ My “Elite AI Designer” Rules

If I were writing the commandments for another AI building this:

1. Never optimize for storing information.

Optimize for recovering value from information later.

2. Never make the user organize everything.

Let the AI organize.

3. Never make the user remember what they already told the AI.

The AI should remember.

4. Never make search depend on exact words.

Search meaning.

5. Never turn the product into a folder hierarchy.

Build relationships.

6. Never confuse popularity with intelligence.

Measure usefulness.

7. Never expose private intelligence by default.

Privacy is foundational.

8. Never let a Smart Note become dead.

Every note should remain connectable to future intelligence.

9. Never make the AI merely summarize.

Make it distill, compare, challenge, connect and compound.

10. Never destroy the house to renovate one room.

Your existing Adaptive Reconstruction + Surgical Evolution principle is exactly right.

11. Never declare completion from source code.

Prove:

source → artifact → deployment → runtime → user experience.

12. Make the user's intelligence more valuable every day.

That last one is the North Star.

